bg3le Ext.UI: Noesis objects reach Lua as userdata that hold a reference

Fixes the SIGSEGV in l_type_name (HANDOFF §4 bug 1, research/impl-se.md): push_object()
handed Noesis objects to Lua as light userdata with no reference, so a proxy could outlive
its object (the dialogue page frees its answers' view models when it re-templates).

- push_object(): a full userdata box per object, cached by address in a weak registry
  table (stable identity), taking AddReference() on BaseComponents; __gc queues Release().
- Releases are drained on the UI thread from the View::Update hooks (noesis_ui.cpp);
  without the hook they happen at once.
- __tostring prints "userdata: %p" of the Noesis pointer, as a light userdata did.
- object_arg(): accepts the box and, as before, light userdata; checks that the vtable's
  first three slots point into the game's or libbg3le's code before any virtual call.
- UiInstantiate: the box adopts Construct()'s creation reference.

Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6). Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
